-- Passage rg9-literary-structure-pov-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('af39d5ce-0be5-5dbf-b7b4-3931e2164528', 'rg9-literary-structure-pov-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Launch Day$q$, $q$Ten: we tape the last seam twice,
check the camera, check the string,
and Ms. Ocampo reads the wind
off a phone held like a compass.

Eight: the helium tank sighs
and the balloon begins to rise
from a puddle of white plastic
into something with a shape.

Seven: someone's little brother asks
if it is going all the way to space.
Nobody answers yes or no.
We just tie the knot again.

Four: the balloon leans over us,
white and wider than the van,
pulling at our hands as if
it already knows the way.

One: we let go together,
and for a while we all look up,
and then the sky is only sky
and we are twelve people in a field.

Up here the field is a green stamp.
The van is a grain of rice.
The cold arrives like news,
and the thin air hums against my skin.
The camera, blinking, keeps the record
of rivers bending like dropped string
and of a town that never thought to look up
at the moment I went by.$q$, 'draft')
