-- Passage rg9-literary-structure-pov-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('687004f3-c787-52af-8d99-1ff8d5354854', 'rg9-literary-structure-pov-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Recital, Two Seats$q$, $q$I. From the Stage

The lights are warmer than I practiced for.
My bow is ready, and my hands are not.
Measure twelve arrives the way a curb does
when you are reading while you walk:
I miss it, and the wrong note rings
out over every folded program.
I keep going because the music keeps going.
I do not look up. I count. I finish.
I bow to a sound I cannot hear as clapping,
only as the noise of my mistake
repeated by four hundred hands.

II. From Row F

She plays the way she practiced in the hall,
the cello leaning into her like a friend.
I know this piece by heart by now,
from every evening through her bedroom door.
Around measure twelve, a note goes sideways,
and for a breath her shoulders rise
and then, I watch it, they come down.
She does not stop. She does not hurry.
I have heard grown players fall apart for less.
When she bows, I stand up first,
not because of the note
but because of what she did after it,
and the whole row stands up behind me.$q$, 'draft')
