   $q$What does the speaker in Part II notice that the speaker in Part I does not mention?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That the audience was laughing at the mistake","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"That the wrong note happened at measure twelve","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"That the cellist's shoulders rose and then came down as she kept playing calmly","is_correct":true},{"text":"That the stage lights were warmer than expected","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That the cellist's shoulders rose and then came down as she kept playing calmly$q$, $q$Only the listener sees the cellist's shoulders "rise / and then... come down," a sign of her recovery. Both speakers mention measure twelve, so that is not the difference.$q$, 'draft', '687004f3-c787-52af-8d99-1ff8d5354854')
