  ('c864d420-2167-5d9a-907a-dd2572cd93ba', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-literary-structure-pov'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the meaning of the applause change between the two sections?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In Part I, there is no applause at all, but in Part II the audience claps for the note.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"In both sections, the applause is polite but shows that the audience is disappointed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"In Part I, the cellist hears it as her mistake repeated, but in Part II it honors how she recovered.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In Part I, the applause celebrates a perfect performance, but in Part II it is only polite.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In Part I, the cellist hears it as her mistake repeated, but in Part II it honors how she recovered.$q$, $q$The cellist hears "my mistake / repeated by four hundred hands," while the listener stands "not because of the note / but because of what she did after it." The two views reveal what each speaker can and cannot know.$q$, 'draft', '687004f3-c787-52af-8d99-1ff8d5354854')
