   $q$How does the limited point of view help create the mystery?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hides Rafael's thoughts, so readers cannot tell what he suspects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Readers know only what Rafael knows, so they share his mistaken guess until the truth appears.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It lets readers hear the boy's thoughts, so they know he is innocent from the start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-point-of-view"},{"text":"It lets readers see Dr. Amadi taking the fossil, so they know the answer early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Readers know only what Rafael knows, so they share his mistaken guess until the truth appears.$q$, $q$Because the story follows only Rafael, readers do not see Dr. Amadi borrow the fossil and are drawn into his suspicion. Rafael's thoughts are shown, not hidden.$q$, 'draft', 'f4a6e09b-cf9f-5919-9624-b868b7223bd4')
