   $q$What is the main effect of telling this story in the second person?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It makes the story sound like a set of travel instructions for visiting Ghana.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It keeps the reader at a distance so the character's feelings stay hidden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It lets the reader hear every relative's private thoughts about the visit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-omniscient"},{"text":"It places the reader inside the character's experience of being between two names and two places.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It places the reader inside the character's experience of being between two names and two places.$q$, $q$Saying "you" puts the reader in the character's shoes as he learns to answer to Kwabena. It brings readers closer, not further away, and does not reveal relatives' thoughts.$q$, 'draft', '23ce4e8e-1ef2-5e5a-9ca0-c6c80479b761')
